{"id":"b965ee564d1897fdaeddaeceecc316aa15a45312","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"b965ee564d1897fdaeddaeceecc316aa15a45312","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".agents/skills/transformers-upgrade/SKILL.md","lines":["@@ -121,6 +121,9 @@ For each deleted config:"," Deleted processors follow the same steps in"," `vllm/transformers_utils/processors/__init__.py`."," ","+Before merging, rebase and grep again for the old field names: PRs that land","+in between still read them.","+"," Done when every line of the inventory output is deleted, or kept with a"," reason that meets the bar in step 2. The PR also carries the config diff"," results and evals for any changed values.","@@ -128,13 +131,15 @@ results and evals for any changed values."," ## Upstreaming hazards"," "," Upstream configs are `@strict` dataclasses. Checkpoint keys upstream does not","-declare survive as plain attributes. Defaults that only vLLM sets, and values","-vLLM derives, vanish.","+declare survive as plain attributes, but only when the checkpoint sets them.","+Defaults that only vLLM sets, and values vLLM derives, vanish."," "," | Hazard | Signal | Fix |"," | --- | --- | --- |"," | Upstream consumes legacy keys | `__post_init__` pops keys the model reads (`deepseek_v4` `compress_ratios`) | Read the upstream replacement (`layer_types`, `mlp_layer_types`, per-layer `rope_parameters`) |"," | Renamed or dropped fields | Diff shows `<MISSING>` for a field the model reads | Read the upstream name; derive dropped flags from what implies them (`enable_moe_block` from `num_experts`) |","+| Undeclared field without a default | `config.x` raises `AttributeError` for configs that omit `x`, e.g. minimal test configs (A.X-K1 `scoring_func`). Dumps of real checkpoints miss it | Upstream ignoring `x` usually means vLLM can stop reading it; if vLLM truly needs it, read `getattr(config, \"x\", <old default>)` |","+| Top-level config stops forwarding | The vendored top-level config forwarded reads to `text_config`; upstream does not. `getattr(config, \"x\", default)` silently takes the default, e.g. on MTP draft configs from `SpeculativeConfig.hf_config_override`, which the dumps do not build | Read from `get_text_config()`; grep `getattr` reads of every field, including speculative-decoding paths |"," | Type check on the config | `ctx.get_hf_config(SomeConfig)` relies on the vendored base class | Accept the upstream class too, e.g. a `Cosmos3ProcessingInfo` overriding `get_hf_config` |"," | Remote code takes over | Checkpoint `config.json` has `auto_map`; with `--trust-remote-code`, the hub class replaces the native one once vLLM stops registering its own | Check the remote class loads; if not, register the upstream class for that `model_type` |"," | Read-only upstream fields | Properties or derived fields break subclasses and `hf_overrides` (`nemotron_h` `hybrid_override_pattern`) | Override the source field (`layers_block_type`) instead |","@@ -159,10 +164,10 @@ Version gates from the inventory need a decision:"," - **Patches citing a Transformers issue or PR:**","     - Delete the patch when its fix is in the floor release.","     - For an issue, find the PR that closed it and check that PR. A closed","-      issue is not a fixed one: #43329 was closed while the bug was still in","-      5.16.1.","+      issue is not a fixed one: issues get closed while the bug is still in","+      the release.","     - Re-run the patched behaviour before deleting. A fix in the release does","-      not always cover vLLM's path: #47924 made Emu3's processor add BOS, but","+      not always cover vLLM's path: Emu3's processor gained BOS upstream, but","       vLLM tokenizes without the processor.","     - Links that only explain a design choice (e.g. a float32 RoPE note) are","       not patches; leave them.","@@ -176,3 +181,11 @@ Version gates from the inventory need a decision:"," "," Add `tests/models/test_initialization.py -k \"<archs>\"` where a GPU is"," available, and a model eval for any model whose resolved config changed.","+","+Models in `vllm/models/` are high priority: whenever their config or model","+code changes, run GSM8k (`tests/evals/gsm8k/`) and GPQA Diamond","+(`tests/evals/gpt_oss/`) on `main` and the branch, even when the dumps show","+no diff, and put both scores in the PR. FlashInfer autotuning picks kernel","+tactics afresh on every server start, which moved DeepSeek-V4-Flash GSM8k by","+about 1 point; pass `--kernel-config '{\"enable_flashinfer_autotune\": false}'`","+to both servers so greedy outputs are comparable."],"additions":18,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/config/test_model_arch_config.py","lines":["@@ -519,7 +519,8 @@ def test_deepseek_v4_convertor_splits_vision_architecture():","     text-only DeepSeek-V4; the convertor routes it to the VL wrapper class","     by rewriting hf_config.architectures (model-class resolution reads the","     raw attribute).\"\"\"","-    from vllm.transformers_utils.configs.deepseek_v4 import DeepseekV4Config","+    from transformers import DeepseekV4Config","+","     from vllm.transformers_utils.model_arch_config_convertor import (","         DeepseekV4ModelArchConfigConvertor,","     )"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/distributed/test_eplb_spec_decode.py","lines":["@@ -7,12 +7,12 @@"," import lm_eval"," import pytest"," import torch","+from transformers import DeepseekV4Config"," "," from tests.utils import large_gpu_mark"," from vllm.distributed.eplb.eplb_state import EplbState"," from vllm.models.deepseek_v4.common.eplb_util import dspark_draft_supports_eplb"," from vllm.platforms import current_platform","-from vllm.transformers_utils.configs.deepseek_v4 import DeepseekV4Config"," from vllm.v1.worker.gpu.eplb_utils import (","     EPLBController,","     draft_model_supports_eplb,","@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ def _make_dsv4_dspark_hf_config() -> DeepseekV4Config:","         vocab_size=256,","         n_mtp_layers=2,","         enable_con